diff --git a/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md b/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4d5b006
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+# Inventory panel: baked images
+
+These are the visuals from the inventory panel design (`design/figma/inventory-panel.json`,
+screen `12:340`, Slot set `20:1`) that are uploaded as images instead of built from UI objects.
+Everything else is built natively (see the end of this file).
+
+All ids live in `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/InventoryAssets.luau` and are
+placeholders (`rbxassetid://0`) for now. Until a real id is in, the panel draws a fallback: a
+rounded swatch in the block's color instead of Block Art, an "X" text glyph on the close button,
+and no lock icon or hex pattern.
+
+**Export scale: 2x.** The UI is authored at 1080p and `Screen.MaxScale` grows it up to 2x on a 4K
+screen, so 2x keeps every image sharp at its largest. Every sheet is under 1024 px per side, so
+Roblox stores it at full resolution.
+
+**Every export:** PNG with a transparent background, and alpha bleed on (the edge color carried
+into the transparent pixels). Without it, Roblox turns transparent pixels black on upload and soft
+edges get a dark fringe when scaled. Upload under the account or group that owns the experience.
+
+| # | Asset | Figma source | Export size | Upload as |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Hex Pattern tile | `40:78` (group of 35 `Hexagon` vectors) | 224 x 384 | One image |
+| 2 | Block Art sheet | `Block Art` in each slot: `40:0`, `40:4`, `40:8`, `40:12`, `40:16`, `40:20`, `40:24`, `40:28`, `40:33`, `40:38` | 800 x 320 | One sheet, 10 cells |
+| 3 | Icon sheet | `Icon/Close` `40:80`, `Icon/Lock` `40:30` | 128 x 64 | One sheet, 2 cells |
+
+## 1. Hex Pattern tile
+
+**What it is.** The faint honeycomb behind the panel's content: white hexagons, 112 x 128 each,
+2 px centered strokes, in rows 96 apart with every other row shifted 56, at 6% group opacity.
+
+**Why baked.** It's 35 vectors of decoration that never changes. Built from UI objects it would be
+dozens of frames, each costing layout and draw work every frame; one tiled image is a single small
+texture.
+
+**Export.** One seamless tile, the smallest piece that repeats: **112 x 192 at 1x, exported at 2x
+= 224 x 384.**
+
+- The pattern repeats every 112 px across and 192 px down, so any 112 x 192 window is seamless.
+  Use the window that starts at the pattern's origin in Roblox: frame coordinates **x 602 to 714,
+  y 352 to 544** (the panel's top-left at 600, 350, plus the 2 px border the pattern sits inside).
+- In Figma: draw a 112 x 192 frame at that spot with **Clip content** on, put copies of every
+  hexagon that overlaps it inside, and set their opacity to **100%** (the 6% is applied in
+  Roblox). Keep the strokes white, 2 px, centered. Export the frame at 2x.
+- Check the seams by laying four copies of the PNG in a 2 x 2 grid: the lines should run on
+  without a break or a doubled stroke.
+
+**Drawn in Roblox.** `HexPattern`, an `ImageLabel` under the panel, behind the content:
+
+- `ScaleType = Tile`, `TileSize = UDim2.fromOffset(112, 192)` (offsets, so the pattern keeps its
+  density at any panel size)
+- `ImageColor3` white, `ImageTransparency = 0.94` (the 6% group opacity)
+- Inset 2 px on every side, inside the panel border, with its own `UICorner` of 14 (the panel's
+  16 minus the inset), since a parent's `UICorner` doesn't clip children
+
+## 2. Block Art sheet
+
+**What it is.** The picture of each block type in its slot: 56 x 56, image fill with **Fit**, with
+a drop shadow (black, 40% alpha, offset 0, 4, blur 8). Ten block types, all shown together.
+
+**Why baked.** Block art is illustration, and the shadow follows the art's shape, which
+`UIShadow` can't do (it shadows only the frame's box). So the shadow is baked into each picture.
+The ten show together every time the panel opens, so they share one sheet: one fetch, one texture,
+and they appear at once.
+
+**Export.**
+
+- Each cell is **80 x 80 at 1x = 160 x 160 at 2x**: the 56 x 56 art at **(12, 8)** in the cell
+  (24, 16 at 2x), so the shadow has 8 px above and to the sides and 16 px below it before the cell
+  edge. The shadow reaches at most 12 px below the art, so cell edges stay transparent and
+  neighbors can't bleed into each other.
+- Export the art with its shadow at **100% opacity**. Ice, Lamp, and Gold sit inside a locked
+  slot's Content frame at 40% opacity in the file; export the `Block Art` rectangle itself, or set
+  that frame to 100% first. Roblox applies the dimming.
+- Lay the cells on a **5 x 2 grid, 800 x 320**, in hotbar order (the order of `BlockTypes.List`):
+
+  | Cell | Block | Node | Rect offset (px) |
+  |---|---|---|---|
+  | 0 | Brick | `40:0` | 0, 0 |
+  | 1 | Dirt | `40:4` | 160, 0 |
+  | 2 | Grass | `40:8` | 320, 0 |
+  | 3 | Window | `40:12` | 480, 0 |
+  | 4 | Wood | `40:16` | 640, 0 |
+  | 5 | Stone | `40:20` | 0, 160 |
+  | 6 | Sand | `40:24` | 160, 160 |
+  | 7 | Ice | `40:28` | 320, 160 |
+  | 8 | Lamp | `40:33` | 480, 160 |
+  | 9 | Gold | `40:38` | 640, 160 |
+
+  Every rect is 160 x 160. Keep its own colors (it's multicolor art, not tinted).
+
+**Drawn in Roblox.** `BlockArt`, an `ImageLabel` in each slot:
+
+- `Size` 80 x 80 at **(8, 8)** in the 96 x 96 slot, which puts the 56 px art at (20, 16) as in
+  the design
+- `ImageRectOffset` from the table, `ImageRectSize = (160, 160)`, `ScaleType = Fit`
+- `ImageTransparency = 0.6` on a locked slot (the Locked variant's 40% content opacity), else 0
+
+Adding a block type means adding a cell: an 11th fits on a third row (800 x 480). Re-uploading
+gives a new id; update `BLOCK_SHEET_ID` and `BLOCK_CELLS`.
+
+## 3. Icon sheet
+
+**What it is.** The two glyphs: the close cross (20 x 20, in the round close button) and the
+padlock (24 x 24, on locked slots). Both are filled with Text/Primary (`#F5F6FA`) and show on the
+panel together.
+
+**Why baked.** Icons are vector shapes that Roblox UI objects can't draw. One color each, so they
+are exported **white** and tinted in Roblox, which lets one image serve any color or state.
+
+**Export.**
+
+- Two **64 x 64** cells side by side: **128 x 64**, white glyphs on transparent.
+- Each glyph fills the **60 x 60 square at its cell's center** (2 px clear on every side, so
+  neighbors don't bleed in when scaled): close at 3x (20 to 60), lock at 2.5x (24 to 60). Both
+  are above the 2x minimum.
+
+  | Cell | Icon | Node | Rect offset (px) | Rect size (px) |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|
+  | 0 | Close | `40:80` | 2, 2 | 60, 60 |
+  | 1 | Lock | `40:30` | 66, 2 | 60, 60 |
+
+**Drawn in Roblox.** An `ImageLabel` each, `ScaleType = Fit`, `ImageColor3 = Text/Primary`:
+
+- Close: 20 x 20, centered in the 44 x 44 close button
+- Lock: 24 x 24, centered across the slot and 10 px above its center (as in the design), shown
+  only on locked slots
+
+## Built natively (not images)
+
+For reference, everything else in the design is UI objects, because each one is something Roblox
+draws directly or changes with state:
+
+| Visual | Built with |
+|---|---|
+| Panel fill `#171A26` | `BackgroundColor3`, transparency 0.04 (see background blur) |
+| Panel 16 px corners, 2 px inside border `#3A4060` | `UICorner`, `UIStroke` `Inner` |
+| Panel drop shadow (0, 12, blur 32, 45%) | `UIShadow`, not shown behind the see-through panel |
+| Panel background blur 24 | Not possible per frame in Roblox: the fill is more opaque instead (Figma alpha 0.92, used 0.96) |
+| Slot vertical gradient `#2B3150` to `#20253B`, 12 px corners | `UIGradient` (rotation 90), `UICorner` |
+| Slot border: 1 px inside `#3A4060`; selected 3 px outside `#FFC83C` | One `UIStroke`, bound to the state |
+| Selected glow (`#FFC83C`, 55%, blur 16, spread 2) | `UIShadow` that fades in and out |
+| Text shadows on title and counts | `UIShadow` in text mode |
+| Close button (white 8%, circle) | `TextButton` with `UICorner` of 50% |
+| Equip button gradient `#FFD25A` to `#FF9F1C`, inner shadow (0, -3, 25%) | `UIGradient`, inset `UIShadow` |
+| All text | `TextLabel`s in Builder Sans, which Roblox ships |
